 61NI c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2013Sc06:                          
 61NI2c  Phys Rev C 87, 034306 (2013); and 2013ScZZ:                            
 61NI3c  Submission to XUNDL database, March 14, 2013                           
 61NI c  Compiled by E. Thiagalingam and B. Singh (McMaster), May 10, 2013      
 61NI c  Neutron adding reactions                                               
 61NI c  E(d)=10 MeV, E(|a)=38 MeV from Yale tandem accelerator of WNSL         
 61NI2c  facility. Measured proton, {+3}He spectra, |s(|q), spectroscopic       
 61NI3c  factors C{+2}S using a split-pole Enge spectrograph. FWHM |?33 keV for 
 61NI4c  protons and |?50 keV for {+3}He. Target=204 |mg/cm{+2} thick 99.7%     
 61NI5c  enriched. Deduced levels, J, |p. DWBA analysis. Comparison with        
 61NI6c  shell-model calculations.                                              
 61NI c  The uncertainties are estimated to be |?4% for |s>1 mb/sr, |?7% for    
 61NI2c  0.1<|s< 1.0 mb/sr, and |?18% for |s<0.1 mb/sr at their respective      
 61NI3c  maxima. The uncertainties arising from possible contaminants or        
 61NI4c  previously unidentified states for very weak transitions could be      
 61NI5c  |?0.02 mb/sr.                                                          
